oaded file. This allowed an attacker to upload arbitrary file types. The fix corrects the field name to `'picture'` so the mime-type and extension checks take effect, and adds `required` to ensure a file must be present.\n\n2. **CWE-22 (Path Traversal)** — The original code used `$file->getClientOriginalName()` (fully attacker-controlled) directly in the filename passed to `->move()`. An attacker could include `../` sequences in the filename (e.g., `../../app/shell.php`), causing the file to be written outside the intended `public_path('images/...')` directory. The fix replaces this with `$file->getClientOriginalExtension()` + `uniqid()`, giving the attacker no control over the path or base filename.\n\n### Verdict\n\nThis is a security vulnerability fix.\n\nVULNERABILITY_FOUND: yes\nCWE_ID: CWE-434, CWE-22\nCWE_NAME: Unrestricted Upload of File with Dangerous Type, Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')\n", "output_dir": "/home/medo/laMiaTesi/agentAnalysisDocker/outputs/polito_deepseek-v4/SMEWebify__WebErpMesv2/c9e7f4a85aeb/agent2", "created_at": "2026-08-07T09:37:16.317616+00:00"}
