cking), but it was missing `IniFile`, creating an exploitable gap.\n\n4. **Impact - Information disclosure**: An attacker exploiting this missing blocklist entry could achieve unauthorized arbitrary file reads from the server, potentially leaking database credentials, application secrets, configuration, or other sensitive data.\n\n### CWE Classification\n\nThe most specific CWE describing this defect is **CWE-184 (Incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs)** — the code uses an allow/blocklist approach to filter dangerous JDBC parameters, but the list was incomplete. The consequence is **CWE-200 (Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor)**, since the practical impact is reading arbitrary files via the `IniFile` JDBC parameter.\n\n---\n\nVULNERABILITY_FOUND: yes\nCWE_ID: CWE-184, CWE-200\nCWE_NAME: Incomplete List of Disallowed Inputs, Exposure of Sensitive Information to an Unauthorized Actor\n", "output_dir": "/home/medo/laMiaTesi/agentAnalysisDocker/outputs/polito_deepseek-v4/dataease__dataease/8f1c21834a62/agent1", "created_at": "2026-08-07T12:36:59.061924+00:00"}
