s local services on the server\n- Serve a redirect to `http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/` — exfiltrate cloud metadata (AWS/GCP metadata endpoint)\n- Serve a redirect to `http://192.168.1.1/internal` — probe internal network resources\n\nAdditionally, there was no limit on redirect chains, enabling infinite redirect loops.\n\n**How the fix works (after):**\n\n1. Uses `redirect: \"manual\"` to prevent automatic redirect following\n2. Manually walks redirect chains (up to 10 redirects)\n3. Calls `validateSafeUrl()` on **every** URL, including each resolved redirect target, before fetching it\n4. Removes the now-redundant `validateSafeUrl()` calls from `getUrlAsDoc()` and `getChildUrlsRecursive()` (since validation is now done inside `fetchWithTimeout` for all URLs)\n\n### CWE Classification\n\nThe primary vulnerability is **SSRF**, where redirect-based bypass allows the document loader to be tricked into accessing internal/private network resources.\n\nVULNERABILITY_FOUND: yes\nCWE_ID: CWE-918\nCWE_NAME: Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF)\n", "output_dir": "/home/medo/laMiaTesi/agentAnalysisDocker/outputs/polito_deepseek-v4/langchain-ai__langchainjs/2812d2b2b9fd/agent2", "created_at": "2026-08-07T14:00:04.715310+00:00"}
