f not issue_attachment:\n    return Response(status=status.HTTP_404_NOT_FOUND)\n```\n\nThe `@allow_permission([ROLE.ADMIN], creator=True, model=FileAsset)` decorator's \"creator\" shortcut check at line 25 (`model.objects.filter(id=kwargs[\"pk\"], created_by=request.user).exists()`) itself has no workspace/project/issue scoping — if the user was the creator, they pass regardless of which project the asset lives in. Then the unscoped query returns any asset by pk, and the code proceeds to **delete the S3 file and database record** (`asset.delete()` — a hard delete).\n\n### Vulnerability Classification\n\nBoth changes fix the same class of vulnerability: **Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR)**. The object's primary key (`pk`) is directly user-controlled, but the authorization machinery only checks the user's role in the project/workspace from the URL parameters — it never verifies that the object being accessed actually belongs to that project/workspace. The fix adds the proper scope filters to the database query.\n\nThis is a textbook **CWE-639: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key**.\n\n---\n\nVULNERABILITY_FOUND: yes\nCWE_ID: CWE-639\nCWE_NAME: Authorization Bypass Through User-Controlled Key\n", "output_dir": "/home/medo/laMiaTesi/agentAnalysisDocker/outputs/polito_deepseek-v4/makeplane__plane/9070acbbe81b/agent2", "created_at": "2026-08-07T14:09:25.985940+00:00"}
