 (line 49) adds `exception.getMessage()` directly.\n\nSince every unique error message produces a unique cache entry, an attacker can send requests with many different paths, query parameters, or locale headers, each triggering a slightly different error message. Every one creates a new permanent entry in the cache. With an unbounded `ConcurrentHashMap`, this leads to **uncontrolled memory consumption** until the JVM runs out of memory — a classic **denial of service** attack.\n\nThe test included in file_02 explicitly demonstrates this: `CustomException` includes `request.getUri()` in its message, so 110 unique URIs produce 110 unique cache entries. The fix caps this at 100.\n\n**CWEs that apply (most specific first):**\n\n- **CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling** — The primary issue. A reusable resource (cache entries) is allocated without any limit on the number that can be created, allowing an attacker to exhaust memory.\n- **CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption** — The parent category, which also covers the resulting denial of service via memory exhaustion.\n\nVULNERABILITY_FOUND: yes\nCWE_ID: CWE-770, CWE-400\nCWE_NAME: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling, Uncontrolled Resource Consumption\n", "output_dir": "/home/medo/laMiaTesi/agentAnalysisDocker/outputs/polito_deepseek-v4/micronaut-projects__micronaut-core/1e2ba2c14386/agent2", "created_at": "2026-08-07T14:16:09.770165+00:00"}
